  "author": "matthuang",
  "author_name": "Matt Huang",
  "text": "If you’re using stablecoins for real-world use cases, it’ll soon be unthinkable that they aren’t private.\n\nToo much of crypto relies on pseudonymity instead of privacy, especially in the age of AI as it becomes easier to track and correlate transactions onchain.\n\nTempo has been working on Tempo Zones as a scalable, technically nuanced, and highly practical solution to onchain privacy.\n\nAnd the first Tempo Zone is now live with Deel, adding privacy to their global contractor payouts.\n\nWe all want real-world flows to scale onchain, and privacy is a clear prerequisite to that. The Tempo team has worked hard to craft a practical solution and if you’re interested in learning more, please reach out to the team!",
